TEXT 568 -48 Left 2 !.inc library.mod
TEXT 112 504 Left 0 ;NMOS: very large width for fast discharge (lower ON-resistance),\nsince we have a very short pulse
TEXT 144 160 Left 0 ;PMOS: 1x larger width to get 1*Iref\n(to then make the slave PMOS charge the cap -slower-)
TEXT 744 224 Left 0 ;PMOS: to avoid Channel Length Modulation, increase lengths\nTransistor longer to increase its output resistance\n \nset to 2u to increase r_o ~6x
TEXT 688 424 Left 1 ;time to reach comp threshold: t (set in project cosntraints)\nthreshold voltage for comp: V_th (to compute)\ncurrent mirror ratio: k = 1 (1:1)\n \nt = ( C * V_th ) / ( k * Iref )     => pulse width is directly inversely proportional to Iref!\n \nif we take t=4.5us for Iref=1uA, we can use a V_th=1.65V as it's\nthe switching point of an inverter, we get then a C/k ratio of 2.727pF\nif we keep our k=1 we can then know we need to use a 2.727pF cap value\n \nBUT it's slower than supposed to (0.4544us rather than 0.5us for 9uA => 0.5/0.4544=1.10035),\nso lets use 2.727pF * 1.10035 = 3pF => adjusted value for the cap\n \nextra fine-tuning: 9uA * 0.4942us = 4.4478, 1uA * 4.42us = 4.42 => ratio=4.4339, we want it at 4.5\n=> 4.5/4.4339 = 1.0149 -> C = 3pF * 1.0149 ~= 3.045pF => fine-tuned value for the cap
TEXT 344 248 Center 0 ;1/1 ratio\n<------------>
